{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"2d74ba91c037b541435a73fe339f63d653ed0e6ea3d55e5af24e4d680ba99c0d","packTokens":1298,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":162,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":492,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":538,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Write its sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"The app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true, so no test may count on those rows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"The web app is built in its own repo; do not build screens here.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"The product stories describe behaviors beyond the locked API contract, while the final instruction says to implement the contract exactly. When a story requires behavior the contract does not define, which scope should govern?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Implement only operations and behavior defined by the locked OpenAPI contract; do not add uncontracted behavior.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"For sample rows that refer to one another, should the seeder create compatible references, or may it seed each table independently?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Create compatible references between related sample rows.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"The contract includes an operation to return a configured staff identity-provider authorization URL, but the provider and source of that configuration are not identified here. What should the API use?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the existing staff identity provider and supply its authorization URL and token-validation settings through deployment configuration.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"When demo seeding is disabled and a database table has no records, should list operations return an empty list or provide sample rows without persisting them?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Return an empty list when the database has no matching records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"The staff identity-provider URL and token-validation settings will come from deployment configuration. What should happen if required settings are missing or invalid?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail application startup with a clear configuration error.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement only the Meridian API operations and behavior defined in the OpenAPI contract, retain the root health, OpenAPI-document, and Swagger UI routes, and conform to the contract’s request, response, authentication, authorization, filtering, and scope requirements.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Persist business-data changes in the configured PostgreSQL database and enforce lifecycle constraints, including creating receipts with Quarantined status and rejecting changes to packed customer orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Run the demo seeder at startup only when `Seed:Demo` is true; when invoked, seed only empty contract-backed tables with two to five contract-example-based rows per table, preserve existing rows, and ensure references resolve.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"When `Seed:Demo` is false or unset, do not run the demo seeder or create demo rows; return empty lists for collection operations with no matching persisted records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Use the existing staff identity provider with authorization URL and token-validation settings from deployment configuration, return the configured URL from the contracted authorization-URL operation, and validate staff tokens using those settings.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Fail application startup with an error identifying the affected setting if a required staff identity-provider authorization URL or token-validation setting is missing or invalid.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Authenticate customer accounts through the contract’s email-and-password and one-time-code flow, associate callers with their declared roles and resource scopes, and authorize operations only for assigned roles and scopes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Create or migrate the PostgreSQL schema to the current contract-backed model at startup, including when the database already exists.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}